GAINLOG — Controlled UI Refinement & Unslop Implementation Brief

1. Objective

Audit and refine the complete GAINLOG interface using the methodology in "heydamir/unslop", adapted specifically to GAINLOG's existing product philosophy, design system, tokens, reusable primitives and mobile-first interaction model.

This is a visual-system refinement, not a redesign or product expansion.

The result must feel deliberately designed for GAINLOG. Do not reproduce another product's visual language, copy unslop's example palette, or impose a generic dashboard aesthetic.

Primary goals, in order:

1. Improve visual hierarchy and information comprehension.
2. Establish one consistent visual language across every screen.
3. Remove unnecessary decoration, visual competition and inconsistent styling.
4. Improve mobile density, alignment, readability and usability.
5. Reduce unnecessary visual motion without harming interaction feedback.
6. Preserve every existing feature, workflow, calculation and data behavior.

Do not stop after producing an audit. Complete the authorized presentation-layer refinements and report what was changed.

