StatCard consistency

All metric cards must share:

- Consistent height and internal alignment within the same grid.
- Consistent value and unit baseline.
- Consistent label and supporting-text hierarchy.
- Consistent padding.
- Intentional use of accents and icons.

Avoid an icon in every card when the label already communicates the metric clearly. Use icons only when they materially improve recognition.

Do not change StatCard's value formatting, unavailable-state behavior, tabular number formatting or data contract.

Section consistency

Use "Section" for meaningful content groups, not as a mandatory wrapper around every small block.

Reserve the larger section treatment for primary modules. Supporting sections should be more compact and visually subordinate.

Avoid creating unnecessary nested section headers.

Accessibility

- Use native buttons for interactive actions.
- Every icon-only button must have an accessible name and a minimum 44 × 44px hit area.
- Maintain visible focus indicators.
- Preserve semantic headings.
- Preserve keyboard interaction.
- Preserve 44 × 44px mobile tap targets where practical.
- Do not rely on hover to expose important controls.
- Preserve non-color status cues.

